<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">health</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">health</ansi> (Hitpoints/HP) stat represents how much damage you can take.

Health will change color to reflect how good/bad your health state is:

<ansi fg="health-100">100%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-90">90%-99%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-80">80%-89%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-70">70%-79%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-60">60%-69%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-50">50%-59%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-40">40%-49%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-30">30%-39%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-20">20%-29%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-10">10%-19%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-0">0%-9%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-dead">dead</ansi>

While you are wounded, healing stops at your wound limit, below your
maximum: <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> shows it as <ansi fg="command">12/16 (limit 13)</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>).

Out of a fight you slowly regain health, but only up to half your
maximum; so do your companions, while you're logged in. Above half, health
comes from your healers (<ansi fg="command">help patch</ansi>), a camp rest or a night at an inn,
which restore you all to full (up to the wound limit). Companions keep
their health when you log out, so it's the same when you come back
(<ansi fg="command">help readiness</ansi>).

At <ansi fg="red">0 HP</ansi>, you will drop to the floor and slowly bleed out.

At <ansi fg="red">-10 HP</ansi>, you will die. When you die, all gear you posess drops to the ground.

Health grows only a little with level: a level 60 fighter has about half
again the health of a level 1 one. Skill, not health, is what levels buy
(<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>).

Maximum health is a base of {{ config "GamePlay.Progression.HPBase" }}, your class's head start, your class's gain
for each level through {{ config "GamePlay.Progression.HPFullLevels" }}, a little over a third of that gain for each later level,
{{ config "GamePlay.Progression.HPPerVitality" }} HP per adjusted Vitality, and health bonuses:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Class</ansi>       <ansi fg="yellow">head start</ansi>   <ansi fg="yellow">a level to 20</ansi>   <ansi fg="yellow">level 1</ansi>   <ansi fg="yellow">level 60</ansi>
  Warrior     10           1               59        88
  Ranger      6            0.8             54        78
  Samurai     6            0.85            54        79
  Rogue       4            0.7             52        73
  Cleric      2            0.6             50        68
  Wizard      0            0.5             48        63
  Witch       1            0.55            49        65
  Shaman      2            0.6             50        68

Those are before Vitality. Fractions accumulate. See <ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>.

